# Titan Stocks runner deployment variables.
#
# Copy this file to ``.env`` and fill in the values. ``.env`` is
# gitignored and must remain mode 0600 or stricter -- the
# registration token lives inside it.
#
# The runner is deployed on a dedicated CI VM; the VM is the
# security boundary. The VM-level network isolation contract and
# the acceptance checks that confirm the VM cannot reach
# protected network ranges or metadata services are documented
# in ``docs/vm-deployment.md``. Confirm the VM firewall follows
# the documented inbound and outbound rules before the first
# ``docker compose up -d``.
#
# ``deploy.sh`` and ``docker compose`` read only the documented
# entries below; arbitrary keys are silently dropped. Adding a new
# variable requires updating both this file and the
# ``ALLOWLIST_KEYS`` array in ``deploy.sh``.
#
# One-command deployment flow
# ===========================
#
#   1. Copy this file to ``.env`` and ``chmod 0600 .env``.
#   2. Set the pinned image digest, the consumer repository URL,
#      the runner identity (``TITAN_RUNNER_NAME`` and
#      ``TITAN_RUNNER_LABELS``), and a fresh GitHub-issued
#      ``TITAN_RUNNER_TOKEN``.
#   3. Run ``docker compose up -d``. The ``register`` sidecar
#      runs first and the long-running listener only starts once
#      registration completes successfully.
#   4. Verify the listener through ``deploy.sh status`` and
#      ``deploy.sh logs``.
#   5. After successful registration, blank the
#      ``TITAN_RUNNER_TOKEN=`` line in this file (or comment it
#      out) and rerun ``docker compose up -d`` so the stopped
#      registration container metadata no longer carries the
#      token. The listener still authenticates with the
#      GitHub-issued long-lived secret persisted in
#      ``titan-runner-state``.
#
# ``TITAN_RUNNER_TOKEN`` is required only on the first
# ``docker compose up -d`` (or after a registration that failed
# or whose identity drifted). GitHub registration tokens expire
# after one hour; refresh the token immediately before the
# bootstrap run.

# Pinned image digest (e.g. ``ghcr.io/pintjesb/titan-stocks-runner@sha256:...``).
# The published image is a multi-platform manifest with both
# ``linux/amd64`` and ``linux/arm64`` entries; ``deploy.sh`` pulls
# the matching native platform from this single digest.
TITAN_RUNNER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/pintjesb/titan-stocks-runner@sha256:replace-with-published-digest

# Repository URL the runner targets.
TITAN_RUNNER_REPO_URL=https://github.com/PintjesB/titan-stocks

# Display name. Defaults to ``titan-ci`` when unset.
TITAN_RUNNER_NAME=titan-ci

# Custom capability labels. GitHub automatically attaches the
# ``self-hosted``, ``linux``, and ``X64``/``ARM64`` labels based
# on the listener's actual platform; the custom-label list
# intentionally omits them so a future architecture migration is
# a GitHub-side change rather than a ``TITAN_RUNNER_LABELS``
# rotation. Defaults to ``titan-ci`` when unset.
TITAN_RUNNER_LABELS=titan-ci

# Short-lived GitHub registration token. Required on the first
# ``docker compose up -d`` (or after a credential rotation). Blank
# the line after successful registration and rerun ``docker compose
# up -d`` so the token leaves the stopped registration container
# metadata. The listener never sees this variable. The token
# never reaches the ``.env.example`` template; ``TITAN_RUNNER_TOKEN``
# is intentionally empty so the committed file is safe to share.
TITAN_RUNNER_TOKEN=

# Optional path overrides. Defaults shown below match the documented layout.
# TITAN_RUNNER_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/titan-runner/state
# TITAN_RUNNER_RUNTIME_DIR=/var/lib/titan-runner/runtime
# TITAN_RUNNER_WORK_DIR=/var/lib/titan-runner/work
# TITAN_RUNNER_BROWSER_DIR=/var/lib/titan-runner/browser
# TITAN_RUNNER_ROOT=/opt/actions-runner
